From 6079aaa2b4e6c82920b82ebdbe6fbe9167180bf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:04:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(setup): lay the part on a G17/G18/G19 plane from a
 picked face or two edges

A setup row on the Setups page gets "Lay on a plane": pick one flat face,
or two straight edges, in the viewport, choose G17 (XY), G18 (ZX) or G19
(YZ), flip it, optionally set the face onto the plane's level, and Apply.
The app computes the rigid turn (pick::lay_on_plane: shortest arc for a
face with the antiparallel case as a half turn about the plane's first
axis; frame-to-frame for two edges, the first edge along X for G17/G18
and Y for G19) and writes it as the setup's part alignment through
AlignPartToSetup::lay_on_plane -> AlignPartToSetup::new (#326), one
undoable command. The work offset is never touched.

Refused by name: a curved or degenerate face, a vertex, a closed or
curved edge, parallel or coincident edges, a wrong pick count, a pick on
the stock or a fixture, a pick no longer in the model. The landing is
proven (normal within 1e-9 rad of the axis) before anything is stored.

The 3-2-1's outward-normal and straight-edge readers take the frame as a
parameter so both features share them; the 3-2-1 is unchanged.

Fixes #330

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
